   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Edit Picture 1 into the next shot. close-up on the face: His hands hold the same lens above the workbench. Preserve the exact existing face, hair, wardrobe, object shape, folds, handle, colours and paper or other rendering material from Picture 1. Keep the same set, lighting, physical conditions and continuity of the action. Use the specified camera viewpoint and framing for the new shot; when a different viewpoint is specified, show the scene from that viewpoint rather than merely cropping Picture 1. Keep people and objects in their consistent positions in the scene, allowing their appearance and screen positions to change with perspective. Visible cast in this shot: Slender build, early twenties, sharp cheekbones framed by dark, tightly braided hair. He wears a tunic of deep indigo linen cinched with a leather sash. He clutches a delicate, glowing crucible.. Physical condition at this instant: Lens held by: the lead. This is the starting pose, before the next action happens. One image, no text."
   ]
